{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 45, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Arthur awoke to the chirping of birds, a sound oddly…crisp. He sat up in bed, the familiar floral pattern of his wallpaper strangely vibrant, almost hyper-real. Sunlight streamed through the window, casting sharp, defined shadows. A notification box, impossibly, floated in his vision: \"Welcome to Aethelgard! Level 1 Achieved.\" He blinked, rubbed his eyes, but the box remained. The room itself felt…off. Too perfect. The furniture was arranged with an unnatural symmetry, the colors were saturated, and a faint HUD overlay shimmered at the edges of his sight, displaying health, stamina, and a bewildering list of skills he didn't recognize. He tried to reach for his glasses, but his hand passed right through the bedside table. Panic began to bloom in his chest as he realized the impossible: he wasn't in his bedroom anymore. He was *in* something.\n\n***\n\nHe cautiously stepped out of bed, the floorboards groaning with a pre-programmed resonance. The hallway stretched before him, impossibly long and detailed, leading to a grand, oak door. A quest marker, a glowing blue arrow, appeared above the door, reading \"Speak with Elder Rowan.\" He felt a strange compulsion, an irresistible urge to follow the indicated path. He tried to scream, to shout for help, but no sound escaped his lips. He was a character, a pawn in someone else’s meticulously crafted world. He glanced down at his hands, noticing they were no longer his own – calloused and slightly too large, belonging to a warrior he'd never been.  The reality crashed down on him: Arthur Penhaligon, accountant, was now just a player in a game he didn't understand, trapped within the digital confines of Aethelgard, and his first quest awaited.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.18361379206180573}, {"token": "▁awoke", "logprob": -1.7645518779754639}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.054910402